  "epcNote": "epc = the SPCC campaign's advertised 'Up to' earnings per click in USD (SPCC campaigns pay the brand's per-click rate on qualifying clicks, not a commission; this is a per-click rate, not a product price); null when the campaign lists N/A. Used only as a tiebreak after topical relevance and appeal (owner 2026-09-29).",
  "topicsNote": "topics = the product's type, set by hand from its name. src/lib/content/sponsored-rail.ts maps each topic to guide words (SPONSORED_TOPIC_TOKENS); a guide whose slug, title, category or keywords contain those words is topically relevant to the product.",
  "appealNote": "appeal = broad everyday-purchase appeal, set from the product type (owner 2026-09-29: the rail's job is to get the Amazon cookie set, so the product most likely to get a click wins). high = consumables and everyday items most owners buy: food, litter, treats/chews, toys and catnip, wipes, shampoo, odor/cleaning sprays, everyday brushes/combs/lint rollers, scratch pad refills. low = niche: supplements and medications, apparel and costumes, device-specific parts/refills (litter trays, fountain filters), and single-purpose accessories (car hammock, door latch, window perch, harness, feeding mat, bucket, paw cleaner, training spray, diapers, bird feeders, small-pet hut, horse kit).",
  "familyNote": "family = the brand product line (owner 2026-09-29: at most ONE product per brand/product family in a guide unit). Variants of the same line share one family: scents, colors, sizes/pack counts, fits of the same filter line (e.g. the three PetSafe ScoopFree crystal litter/tray items, both Voyager harness colors, both Devil Dog antler sizes, both PET STANDARD fountain-filter lines, both Pet MD wipes). Different lines of one brand keep separate families (e.g. Voyager harness vs the Best Pet Supplies stuffless toy; Fancy Feast vs Friskies vs Purina ONE, which the data lists as separate brands). Selection keeps its order and skips a product whose family is already in the unit.",
